
 # Schema /DDL

  Query and what it does :-

  Create a table ->
  CREATE TABLE orders (id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY, customer_id BIGINT, amount DECIMAL(10,2),
  status VARCHAR(20), created_at TIMESTAMP);

  Add a column ->
  ALTER TABLE orders ADD COLUMN currency VARCHAR(3) DEFAULT 'INR';

  Change column type (MySQL syntax; ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE in Postgres) ->
  ALTER TABLE orders MODIFY COLUMN amount DECIMAL(12,2);

  Remove a column ->
  ALTER TABLE orders DROP COLUMN currency;

  Speed up lookups/joins on that column ->
  CREATE INDEX idx_orders_customer_id ON orders(customer_id);

  Index + enforce uniqueness — directly relevant to your idempotency-key work->
  CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_orders_idempotency_key ON orders(idempotency_key);

  Enforce referential integrity ->
  ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT fk_customer FOREIGN KEY (customer_id) REFERENCES customers(id);

  Delete the table entirely (irreversible) ->
  DROP TABLE orders;

